Subject: [PATCH] Port aurora-silicon/m1n1's merged change #35 (cfa4ffc0)

kboot: add J713/T8132 (M4 MacBook Air) boot handoffs

aurora-silicon/m1n1 #35 (aurora-silicon/m4/pr1-basic-bringup), merged
as cfa4ffc0, onto omacom/m1n1 integration/aurora at bc79acc (the RC3
m1n1-aurora pin). It is ported as one commit, the PR's merge diff
against its first parent (git cherry-pick -m 1), and carries these
commits by Eryk Wieliczko:

  f7cbeba9 pmgr: expose ADT consumer power-state checks
  0066b362 kboot: reserve the retained J713 bootloader and firmware heap
  b59b1066 nvme: adopt the J713 ANS session and publish its live resources
  c165398e kboot: refresh T8132 lifecycle SPMI and PMU resources from ADT
  d1a403e6 pcie: hand off selected J713 endpoint rails and DART streams
  e991b303 dapf: initialize only explicitly handed-over active J713 consumers
  a6441e06 display: preserve the J713 DCP session and publish validated mappings
  a925e072 kboot: publish the qualified M4 GPU firmware handoff
  bc331acb doc: describe J713 boot and retained firmware ownership
  a339d9cc kboot: export J713 banked USB3 PHY calibration
  cda8314d dapf: preserve T8132 state without a qualified filter writer

Behaviour is unchanged for every board except apple,j713, which every
new path still requires.

Conflict resolutions. The merge base of bc79acc and cfa4ffc0^1 is
7af7075f; omacom changed these spots after it:

- src/dart.c, src/dart.h: omacom 7e00d548 (Chris Kearney, "dart: restore
  protected M1 DCP table mappings with retained ownership") added
  dart_init_adt_display() where #35 adds dart_set_bypass_fdt(). These
  are independent new functions, so both are kept, omacom's first (it
  needed its closing brace restored between the two).
- src/pmgr.c: omacom 65eb9239/ed5795f2 (Chris Kearney, T8122 PMP)
  added pmgr_gate_fill(), pmgr_adt_gate() and pmgr_device_gate() where
  #35 adds pmgr_adt_is_powered(). Both are kept, omacom's first.
- src/display.c, display_shutdown(): omacom b3572931 (DjDeveloperr, "dcp:
  keep a DCP's buffers and mappings when its firmware does not stop")
  made display_shutdown() return int; #35 adds T8132 to the T8140
  early return, written for the old void function. Resolved as
  "if (chip_id == T8140 || chip_id == T8132) return 0;": #35's
  condition with omacom's return value.
- src/kboot.c, kboot_prepare_dt(): omacom 7e00d548 added a T8103
  inherited-heap block immediately before the T8140 retained-heap
  block; #35 widened that T8140 block's condition to the J713. The
  T8103 block is kept unchanged and is followed by #35's widened
  condition and comment.
- tests/python/test_j700_atc_dp.py: omacom 2d9aec6c (Chris Kearney)
  ends the extracted helper at dt_export_j700_atc()'s own closing
  brace; #35 moved the end marker to the renamed
  dt_copy_atc_t6030_dp_tunables(). omacom's end is kept: it does not
  depend on the next function's name.
- tests/python/test_nvme_adoption.py: omacom ead37bd8 (iconidentify,
  Neo #8) uses failure cases 15-22 for shutdown faults; #35 uses
  15-19 for its T8132 cases. omacom's cases keep their numbers and are
  limited to 15-22; #35's are renumbered 23-27 (15->23, 16->24,
  17->25, 18->26, 19->27) and the loop runs range(28). No assertion is
  changed beyond the numbers.

